&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DIRECTOR, STARLINK PRODUCTION (ASSEMBLY)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly motivated and achievement-oriented leader to own Starlink Product Assembly Production in Bastrop, TX—scaling high-volume manufacturing to fuel global connectivity for millions. This includes oversight and responsibility for Assembly, Test, Manufacturing Engineering, Automation, and Maintenance across high-rate automated mechanical/pick &amp;amp; place, SMT/PCBA, and large electromechanical build production lines. This position plays a critical role in achieving rapid user expansion required for the success of the organization. Ideal candidates have a successful track record of scaling complex operations, leading 200+ person teams, and building cross-functional partnerships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the strategic &amp;amp; tactical execution of Starlink Product Production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead 250+ staff (multiple direct reports) across engineering and operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and mentor high-performing teams of manufacturing, process, and automation engineers to operationalize and continuously improve production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement a development program to enhance the capability of all team members while improving quality and reducing lead time &amp;amp; cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Responsible Engineering teams to embed manufacturability into the design of new products and production lines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure a strong focus is placed on safety and maintain an excellent safety record.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion continuous improvement projects using appropriate metrics &amp;amp; data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use quality metrics to continually improve the quality output of the operation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage resource levels to ensure optimum performance of the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and communicate area status/readiness and risks to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and maintain compliance with internal quality and customer contractual requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a spirit of cooperation and collaboration within and between departments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet tight production schedules to achieve high-rate production, while adapting to changing priorities in a fast-moving environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Think creatively and drive innovation; question the status quo, while following documentation and maintaining prescribed quality standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in a STEM or engineering discipline OR 7+ years of production/manufacturing experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in production/manufacturing/operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in people leadership.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing large teams comprised of engineering and operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thorough knowledge of electronics manufacturing and test techniques.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience monitoring cost and quality (ISO 9000, AS9100) standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and delivering continuous improvement projects within a production environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fast-paced iterative design environments within the consumer electronics, mobile handset, medical devices, or automotive industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to communicate complex concepts, problems, and solutions clearly and effectively to all levels within the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to act and execute in a scrappy, entrepreneurial manner against tight timelines and aggressive schedules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong desire to mentor and grow employees and manage out poor performers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to work extended hours and/or weekends as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to travel as needed, up to 25%.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ITAR REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations, applicant must be a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful, permanent resident (aka green card holder), (iii) Refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) Asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, or be eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State. Learn more about the ITAR &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pmddtc.state.gov/?id=ddtc_kb_article_page&amp;amp;sys_id=24d528fddbfc930044f9ff621f961987&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceX is an Equal Opportunity Employer; employment with SpaceX is governed on the basis of merit, competence and qualifications and will not be influenced in any manner by race, color, religion, gender, national origin/ethnicity, veteran status, disability status, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, mental or physical disability or any other legally protected status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants wishing to view a copy of SpaceX’s Affirmative Action Plan for veterans and individuals with disabilities, or applicants requiring reasonable accommodation to the application/interview process should reach out to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:EEOCompliance@spacex.com&quot;&gt;EEOCompliance@spacex.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PRODUCTION DIRECTOR (STARSHIP)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceX is revolutionizing the space industry by challenging what is possible and relentlessly pursuing continuous improvement to make life multiplanetary. The Starship spacecraft and Super Heavy booster form the most powerful launch system ever developed, designed to carry crew and cargo to Earth orbit, the Moon, Mars, and beyond. As Director of Starship Production at Starbase, you will lead large-scale, multi-disciplinary production teams and complex manufacturing projects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on leadership role that requires diving deep into the unique engineering and production challenges of building flight hardware at unprecedented cadence and scale. You will lead some of the most passionate and capable technicians and engineers on the planet. By driving process excellence, optimizing production systems, and fostering a high-performance culture, you will make a lasting impact on humanity’s journey to space—turning ambitious goals into flight-ready vehicles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the strategic and tactical execution of Starbase Production Operations such that manifest milestones are consistently achieved&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage overall staff and several direct reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate extensively with engineering leaders to ensure vehicle development meets all critical timelines and does not impact schedule to launch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet tight production schedules to achieve high-rate production, while adapting to changing priorities in a fast moving environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain productive relationships and often influence others outside of area of responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a high performing culture whereby people leadership is an essential responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure a strong focus is placed on safety and maintain an excellent safety record&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion continuous improvement projects using appropriate metrics and data sources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a spirit of cooperation and collaboration within and between support departments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Think creatively; question the status quo, while following documentation and maintaining prescribed quality standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in an engineering field or at least 8+ years of experience in a production/military/automotive environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in a manufacturing/engineering leadership role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in a managerial role overseeing indirect reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of building, motivating, mentoring, and coaching high performance manufacturing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical project management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent technical expertise and judgement across multiple engineering disciplines&amp;nbsp;permitting peer-level review of your team’s work product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creative problem solving that can bring multiple disciplines together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to assess risk and make development decisions without all available data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills with direct experience negotiating integrated system trades between various stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with cross-functional teams and external customers or vendors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly detail oriented and passionate about advancing the commercial space industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in a fast-paced, autonomously driven, and demanding start-up atmosphere&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be willing to work extended hours and/or weekends as needed to meet critical deliverable and launch/test schedule timelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to travel for short and extended trips as needed (up to 10% travel)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ITAR REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations, applicant must be a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful, permanent resident (aka green card holder), (iii) Refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) Asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, or be eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State. Learn more about the ITAR &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pmddtc.state.gov/?id=ddtc_kb_article_page&amp;amp;sys_id=24d528fddbfc930044f9ff621f961987&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceX is an Equal Opportunity Employer; employment with SpaceX is governed on the basis of merit, competence and qualifications and will not be influenced in any manner by race, color, religion, gender, national origin/ethnicity, veteran status, disability status, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, mental or physical disability or any other legally protected status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants wishing to view a copy of SpaceX’s Affirmative Action Plan for veterans and individuals with disabilities, or applicants requiring reasonable accommodation to the application/interview process should reach out to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:EEOCompliance@spacex.com&quot;&gt;EEOCompliance@spacex.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SENIOR MANAGER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceX is building and operating combined-cycle gas turbine power plants that must come online, stay online, and perform. This role owns the design and build of the full power plant: gas turbines, mechanical and electrical balance of plant, and everything else that keeps the plant running at rated output, day after day. This is not a desk job. You will be constructing the power plant, owning commissioning in the control room during startup, and in the field troubleshooting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, lead, and develop a multi-disciplinary power plant team spanning gas turbines, mechanical and electrical balance of plant, controls, and commissioning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full lifecycle of gas turbine power generation assets — installation, commissioning, startup, operations, and long-term maintenance — and be accountable for plant availability, reliability, and performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set technical direction and execution plans for commissioning, including combustion tuning, control system checkout, protective relay testing, and performance/reliability run verification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own root-cause analysis and corrective action for turbine trips, forced outages, and performance degradation; drive fixes that prevent recurrence and hold the team to a no-repeat standard&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and continuously improve operating procedures, startup/shutdown sequences, and abnormal operating condition playbooks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary technical and commercial interface with OEMs (GE, Siemens Energy, Mitsubishi Power, Doosan) on warranty issues, LTSA scope, outage planning, and technical issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan, staff, and execute major/minor inspections, hot gas path outages, and combustion inspections in line with OEM maintenance intervals; own outage cost, duration, and quality of return-to-service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive turbine performance analysis (heat rate, capacity factor, degradation curves) to identify efficiency losses and convert findings into funded corrective action&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate across balance-of-plant teams (HRSG, steam turbine, cooling systems, water treatment) to deliver integrated plant performance, not siloed subsystem success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the construction-to-operations handoff with EPC contractors; ensure a clean transition from construction to commercial operation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and own spare parts strategy, critical spares inventory, and maintenance budgets; manage spend against reliability and availability targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, coach, and retain engineers and technicians; set performance standards and grow the next generation of plant leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the power plant organization to internal stakeholders (operations, grid interconnection, commercial, construction) and make timely field decisions under pressure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree and 10+ years of experience working in one or more of the following; or 14+ years of experience working utility-scale gas turbines in commissioning, operations, maintenance, or plant engineering roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of project management experience leading operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of combined-cycle plant systems: gas turbines, HRSGs, steam turbines, generators, and balance-of-plant equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience reading and interpreting P&amp;amp;IDs, single-line diagrams, and turbine control logic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct commissioning or operations leadership experience with GE 7/9HA, Siemens Energy SGT6/8-8000H, Mitsubishi M501/701JAC, or Doosan H-class turbines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with DCS/turbine control platforms (Mark VIe, SPPA-T3000, or equivalent)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with LTSA structures, OEM contract negotiation, and outage scope development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in root-cause failure analysis (RCA/5-Why/Fishbone) for rotating equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with performance monitoring tools and heat balance modeling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to grid interconnection requirements, PPA performance obligations, or capacity market rules&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating power generation with co-located industrial or data center loads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ownership of plant or fleet reliability metrics (availability, forced outage rate, heat rate) and of the budgets that fund them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience standing up a new plant, commissioning organization, or operations team from construction through commercial operation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bias toward action: comfortable making a call in the field without waiting for a committee&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work under pressure during startup, outages, or unplanned events, with a sense of urgency and ownership over outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using SOLIDWORKS, Siemens NX, or similar CAD software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of engineering standards and best practices such as ASME B31.3, ASME BPV Code Section VIII, and AFSPCMAN 91-710&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ITAR REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations, applicant must be a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful, permanent resident (aka green card holder), (iii) Refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) Asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, or be eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State. Learn more about the ITAR &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pmddtc.state.gov/?id=ddtc_kb_article_page&amp;amp;sys_id=24d528fddbfc930044f9ff621f961987&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceX is an Equal Opportunity Employer; employment with SpaceX is governed on the basis of merit, competence and qualifications and will not be influenced in any manner by race, color, religion, gender, national origin/ethnicity, veteran status, disability status, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, mental or physical disability or any other legally protected status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants wishing to view a copy of SpaceX’s Affirmative Action Plan for veterans and individuals with disabilities, or applicants requiring reasonable accommodation to the application/interview process should reach out to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:EEOCompliance@spacex.com&quot;&gt;EEOCompliance@spacex.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Agility’s commercially deployed humanoids operate alongside teams in warehouses, manufacturing facilities, and distribution centers—tackling physically demanding and repetitive tasks while enabling workers to focus on higher-value work. With industry-leading safety standards and years of proven deployment data, we&#39;re pioneering a new era of automation that enhances human potential.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;We are seeking an experienced &lt;strong&gt;Staff Manufacturing Quality Engineer &lt;/strong&gt;to lead factory quality engineering across our final assembly, sub-assembly, and testing operations. In this role, you will hold technical ownership of line quality, process capability, and quality gate containment at our manufacturing facilities. You will partner cross-functionally with Manufacturing Engineering, Advanced Manufacturing, NPI, Supply Chain, and Design Engineering to establish rigorous process controls, qualify production lines, drive defect prevention, and ensure zero-escape assembly for mission-critical electromechanical systems.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own Factory Quality &amp;amp; Yield Performance:&lt;/strong&gt; Establish, monitor, and drive continuous improvement across key manufacturing quality metrics—including First Time Quality (FTQ) First Pass Yield (FPY), Scrap &amp;amp; Rework Rates, and End-of-Line (EOL) failure escape rates across sub-assembly and final integration lines.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Process Characterization &amp;amp; Statistical Control:&lt;/strong&gt; Design and execute Measurement System Analysis (Gage R&amp;amp;R), Process Capability studies (Cp/Cpk), and Statistical Process Control (SPC) charting on critical-to-quality (CTQ) parameters, such as automated torque fastening, press-fits, PCBA flashing, and joint calibration.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion PFMEA &amp;amp; Control Plans:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop, maintain, and rigorously update Process Failure Mode and Effects Analysis (PFMEA) and manufacturing Quality Control Plans (QCP). Ensure lessons learned from field returns (CAPA/RMA) and NPI prototypes are proactively mitigated in line architecture.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own Line 8D &amp;amp; Root Cause Problem Solving:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead cross-functional problem-solving initiatives using 8D, DMAIC, 5-Why, and Fishbone methodologies for chronic manufacturing defects, line stops, and assembly quality escapes, driving verified corrective and preventive actions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NPI to Production Quality Transition:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with NPI and Manufacturing Engineering during build phases (EVT/DVT/PVT) to audit assembly lines, validate line tooling/fixtures, sign off on quality gates, and certify line readiness for commercial rate ramp.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Standardize Quality Work Instructions &amp;amp; Inspection:&lt;/strong&gt; Define and implement standardized incoming/in-process inspection criteria, quality verification fixtures, Go/No-Go tooling, and assembly quality checklists across workstations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Quality Reviews &amp;amp; Pareto Analytics:&lt;/strong&gt; Analyze factory defect trends to publish regular quality Pareto analyses, root-cause summaries, and corrective action status updates to operations and engineering leadership.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt; Bachelor’s degree in Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Industrial &amp;amp; Systems Engineering, Mechatronics, or equivalent technical degree.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 8+ years of hands-on Manufacturing Quality, Quality Engineering, or Advanced Manufacturing experience supporting high-complexity, low-to-mid volume electromechanical systems (Robotics, Automotive/EV, Aerospace, Industrial Automation, or Medical Devices).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process &amp;amp; Tooling Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven expertise implementing quality controls for complex electro-mechanical assemblies, high-torque robotic actuators, precision gearboxes, structural bonded assemblies, wire harnesses, and PCBA/box-build integration.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Statistical &amp;amp; Quality Engineering Toolkit:&lt;/strong&gt; Advanced practitioner in SPC, Gage R&amp;amp;R, Cp/Cpk analysis, PFMEA, Control Plans, IQ/OQ/PQ, and structured problem-solving methodologies (8D, DMAIC, 5-Why, Ishikawa, FTA).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Factory Systems Exposure:&lt;/strong&gt; Direct experience working within Manufacturing Execution Systems (MES), Product Lifecycle Management (PLM), and Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) platforms for quality gate enforcement and traceability.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Certified Quality Engineer (ASQ-CQE), Six Sigma Black Belt (SSBB), or Certified Quality Auditor (CQA).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Experience with functional testing, End-of-Line (EOL) dyno/burn-in testing, and automated optical/laser measurement systems (CMM, Keyence, 3D profiling).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Familiarity with industrial automation and functional safety standards (ISO 9001, IATF 16949, ISO 13849).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Direct experience ramping automated or semi-automated production lines from prototype to volume manufacturing.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Environment &amp;amp; Travel&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Based full-time on-site at our manufacturing facility in Salem, OR, with daily presence on the assembly floor, quality inspection areas, and test bays.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Occasional travel (up to 15%) to regional contract manufacturers, key sub-tier component suppliers, or our Fremont, CA engineering center.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;This is an onsite position at our Salem office.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;The final salary offered to a successful candidate will be dependent on several factors that may include but are not limited to: job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. Agility Robotics is a multi-state employer and this salary range may not reflect positions who work in other locations. These ranges may be modified in the future.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Anticipated Base Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$140,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$182,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;In addition to base pay, our competitive total rewards package consists of the following for full-time employees:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;401(k) Plan:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Includes a 6% company match.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Company stock options.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Insurance Coverage:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;100% company-paid medical, dental, vision, and short/long-term disability insurance for employees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefit Start Date:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Eligible for benefits on your first day of employment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Well-Being Support:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Employee Assistance Program (EAP).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Time Off:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exempt Employees:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Flexible, unlimited PTO and 12 company holidays, including a winter shutdown.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Non-Exempt Employees:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;10 vacation days, paid sick leave, and 12 company holidays, including a winter shutdown, annually.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On-Site Perks:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Catered lunches four times a week and a variety of healthy snacks and refreshments at our Salem and Pittsburgh locations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Parental Leave:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Generous paid parental leave programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Environment:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;A culture that supports flexible work arrangements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth Opportunities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Professional development and tuition reimbursement programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relocation Assistance:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Provided for eligible roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Annual Discretionary Bonus:&lt;/strong&gt; Provided for eligible roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;All of our roles are U.S.-based. Applicants must have current authorization to work in the United States.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Agility Robotics is committed to a work environment in which all individuals are treated with respect and dignity. Each individual has the right to work in a professional atmosphere that promotes equal employment opportunities and prohibits unlawful discriminatory practices, including harassment. Therefore, it is the policy of Agility Robotics to ensure equal employment opportunity without discrimination or harassment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, marital status, citizenship, national origin, genetic information, or any other characteristic protected by law. Agility Robotics prohibits any such discrimination or harassment.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agility Robotics does not accept unsolicited referrals from third-party recruiting agencies.&amp;nbsp; We prioritize direct applicants and encourage all qualified candidates to apply directly through our careers page.&amp;nbsp; If you are represented by a third party, your application may not be considered.&amp;nbsp; To ensure full consideration, please apply directly.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h1 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Mach Industries&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2023, Mach Industries is a rapidly growing defense technology company focused on developing next-generation autonomous defense platforms. At the core of our mission is the commitment to delivering scalable, decentralized defense systems that enhance the strategic capabilities of the United States and its allies. With a workforce of approximately 350 employees, we operate with startup agility and ambition.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our vision is to redefine the future of warfare through cutting-edge manufacturing, innovation at speed, and unwavering focus on national security. We are dedicated to solving the next generation of warfare with lethal systems that deter kinetic conflict and protect global security.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1 data-pm-slice=&quot;0 0 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mach Industries is seeking a Principal Manufacturing Engineer, Energetics to lead the development and industrialization of manufacturing systems for solid rocket motors (SRMs), pyrotechnics, and energetic products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will have end-to-end technical ownership of energetic manufacturing capability, from early manufacturing concepts and process architecture through facility buildout, equipment integration, commissioning, qualification, and production launch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will define how energetic products are manufactured at scale: translating product and process requirements into manufacturing cells, production lines, hazardous-process facilities, equipment specifications, controls architectures, material flows, and commissioning plans.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly cross-functional role requiring coordination across product engineering, manufacturing, automation, facilities, EHS, quality, operations, external A/E firms, equipment OEMs, and systems integrators.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate has personally taken complex manufacturing systems from concept through production and is comfortable operating as the technical DRI for large, multidisciplinary capital projects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manufacturing System &amp;amp; Line Design&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the manufacturing architecture for solid rocket motor, pyrotechnic, and other energetic production lines from raw material receipt through finished-product acceptance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate product requirements and production targets into manufacturing processes, equipment requirements, cycle times, staffing models, material flows, and factory layouts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop process flows, equipment concepts, line balancing, capacity models, manufacturing requirements, and capital equipment roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish equipment boundaries, interfaces, utilities, controls requirements, inspection strategy, and material-handling concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead design reviews including process, equipment, layout, automation, operability, maintainability, and production-readiness reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify manufacturing bottlenecks and develop scalable production architectures capable of supporting significant rate increases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive Design for Manufacturing and Assembly (DFMA) feedback into product development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Energetics Process Industrialization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industrialize manufacturing processes associated with solid rocket motors and pyrotechnic products, including energetic material preparation, mixing, casting/dispensing, curing, machining, assembly, inspection, testing, and material handling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate development processes into robust, repeatable production processes with defined operating windows and acceptance criteria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop process specifications, manufacturing requirements, equipment URS documents, control plans, and qualification strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with EHS and process safety teams to incorporate energetic-material hazards into equipment and process design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive reductions in operator exposure and manual handling through appropriate automation, remote operation, process isolation, and engineered controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Facility &amp;amp; Infrastructure Buildout&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the manufacturing technical owner for new energetic production facilities and major facility expansions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate manufacturing processes into facility requirements including equipment layouts, utilities, hazardous-area requirements, material flows, personnel flows, storage requirements, and operational constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with architects, A/E firms, general contractors, EHS, authorities having jurisdiction, and equipment integrators throughout facility design and construction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in concept design, basis-of-design development, FEED, detailed design, construction, installation, and startup.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure facility design supports production throughput, equipment maintainability, future expansion, safe operations, and efficient material movement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own manufacturing requirements and interfaces between the facility, process equipment, automation systems, utilities, and production operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Capital Equipment &amp;amp; Integration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop technical specifications and requirements for custom and off-the-shelf manufacturing equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead equipment vendor and systems-integrator selection from technical evaluation through execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own technical execution of major manufacturing equipment programs including design reviews, fabrication, integration, installation, and acceptance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with automation engineers and integrators to define controls, robotics, machine vision, data acquisition, traceability, and manufacturing software requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and approve equipment designs for process capability, safety, serviceability, controls architecture, and production readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage technical interfaces across multiple equipment suppliers and integrators to ensure individual systems function as a complete manufacturing line.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commissioning &amp;amp; Production Launch&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own manufacturing equipment commissioning and line startup from installation through production release.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute equipment acceptance and commissioning strategies including FAT, SAT, commissioning, process qualification, and production-readiness activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead equipment debugging, process characterization, capability studies, and production trials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish equipment and process acceptance criteria and drive closure of technical issues identified during commissioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Quality to establish inspection strategies, process controls, traceability, and manufacturing acceptance criteria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive production ramp by identifying and eliminating constraints related to equipment reliability, cycle time, yield, scrap, ergonomics, and process capability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Transition manufacturing systems to site operations and maintenance teams with appropriate documentation, training, spare-parts strategies, and sustainment plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a senior technical authority for energetic manufacturing systems across Mach Industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead multidisciplinary technical decisions spanning manufacturing, automation, facilities, process safety, quality, and operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop manufacturing standards and reusable architectures for future energetic production facilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor manufacturing and automation engineers and raise the technical standard for capital equipment execution across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently identify technical and program risks and drive them to resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate manufacturing strategy, technical tradeoffs, capital requirements, schedule risks, and execution status to engineering and company leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Mechanical Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering, Chemical Engineering, Aerospace Engineering, or a related technical discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in manufacturing engineering, process engineering, industrialization, factory engineering, or capital equipment development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ownership of complex manufacturing equipment or production lines from concept through installation, commissioning, and production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing manufacturing processes and translating them into equipment and facility requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience specifying, procuring, integrating, and commissioning capital equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with equipment OEMs, systems integrators, construction teams, and/or A/E firms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of manufacturing fundamentals including process capability, line balancing, equipment reliability, yield, throughput, and production ramp.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead complex technical programs across multiple engineering disciplines with limited oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience designing, building, commissioning, or operating solid rocket motor, propellant, pyrotechnic, ammunition, warhead, or other energetic-material manufacturing facilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with energetic processes such as material preparation, mixing, casting, dispensing, curing, machining, assembly, inspection, and testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience taking an energetic manufacturing process from development or pilot scale into rate production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with hazardous-process facility design and manufacturing equipment intended for explosive or energetic environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of applicable explosives, fire protection, electrical, process safety, and DoD energetic-manufacturing requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with A/E and EPC organizations on greenfield or brownfield manufacturing facility projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing equipment URS documents, RFQs/RFPs, statements of work, acceptance criteria, and capital project specifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience executing FAT, SAT, commissioning, process qualification, and production acceptance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with automated manufacturing equipment, PLC-controlled systems, robotics, machine vision, and manufacturing data systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building production systems within aerospace, defense, propulsion, munitions, automotive, semiconductor, chemical processing, or similarly demanding manufacturing environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Available to work extended hours and weekends as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ITAR Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations, applicant must be a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful, permanent resident (aka green card holder), (iii) Refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) Asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, or be eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State. Learn more about the ITAR&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pmddtc.state.gov/?id=ddtc_kb_article_page&amp;amp;sys_id=24d528fddbfc930044f9ff621f961987&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Principal&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$180,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$220,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;0 0 []&quot;&gt;At Mach, we believe that compensation is more than just a paycheck. It&#39;s a comprehensive package designed to reward the time, skills, and expertise you bring to our team. We are committed to offering competitive compensation that is equitable, transparent, and aligned with market trends.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Key Elements of Our Compensation Philosophy:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Competitive Salaries&lt;/strong&gt;: We continuously research market rates to ensure our salaries are competitive with those in our industry and geographic location.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance-Based Incentives&lt;/strong&gt;: Our bonus structure is tied to both individual and company performance, creating a win-win scenario that motivates our team members to excel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity Participation&lt;/strong&gt;: We offer stock options or equity to employees, ensuring that you share in the success and growth of the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefit Packages&lt;/strong&gt;: Our benefits include healthcare, dental and vision plans, retirement savings, and paid time off, because we understand that your well-being extends beyond the office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Professional Development&lt;/strong&gt;: We allocate funds for continuing education, training, and career growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transparency&lt;/strong&gt;: We are committed to openness about our compensation tiers and how decisions are made, ensuring trust and mutual respect.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By joining Mach, you’re not just accepting a job—you’re becoming a key part of a team that values your contributions and invests in your growth. Together, we aim to create a rewarding environment that sets the stage for long-term success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Privacy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;To view Mach Industries candidate data privacy policy, please visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://machindustries.com/privacy-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;https://machindustries.com/privacy-policy&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Disclosures&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position may require access to information protected under U.S. export control laws and regulations, including the Export Administration Regulations (EAR) and the International Traffic in Arms Regulations (ITAR).&amp;nbsp; Please note that any offer for employment may be conditioned on authorization to receive software or technology controlled under these U.S. export control laws and regulations without sponsorship for an export license.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mach participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the U.S.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The salary range for this role is an estimate based on a wide range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offers may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and training, critical skills, and business considerations. Highly competitive equity grants are included in most offers and are considered part of Mach’s total compensation package. Mach offers benefits such as health insurance, retirement plans, and opportunities for professional development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mach is an equal opportunity employer committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. All qualified applicants will be treated with respect and receive equal consideration for employment without regard to race, color, creed, religion, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, uniform service, Veteran status, age, or any other protected characteristic per federal, state, or local law, including those with a criminal history, in a manner consistent with the requirements of applicable state and local laws. If you’d like to defend the American way of life, please reach out!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;Space is a warfighting domain. True Anomaly seeks those with the talent and ambition to build the technology that secures it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;OUR MISSION&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;True Anomaly delivers decisive capabilities for space superiority. We build autonomous spacecraft, advanced payloads, mission software, and space-based interceptors — enabling the U.S. and its Allies to secure the space environment and counter threats from the ultimate high ground.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;OUR VALUES&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be the offset.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;We create asymmetric advantages with creativity and ingenuity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What would it take?&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We challenge assumptions to deliver ambitious results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It’s the people.&lt;/strong&gt; Our team is our competitive advantage and we are better together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;BENEFITS &amp;amp; PERKS&lt;/span&gt;*&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Best-in-class healthcare: &lt;/strong&gt;100% company-paid medical, dental, and vision coverage for you and your dependents, with HSA/HRA options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generous time off: &lt;/strong&gt;Flexible Time Off (FTO) for exempt employees, accrued PTO of up to 25 days for non-exempt employees, plus 12 paid holidays; Parental Leave; Sick Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fuel for your day: &lt;/strong&gt;Daily catered lunch and unlimited snacks for in-office employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;And more: &lt;/strong&gt;401(k) retirement plan, fitness reimbursement, and Dog Fridays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity participation: &lt;/strong&gt;Equity is included as part of our total compensation package, giving you an opportunity to share in the company’s success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Do not apply to fixed term and temporary roles&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOUR MISSION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an operations leader to take ownership of the everyday workplace operations at True Anomaly. From office management to culinary, janitorial to groundskeeping to beyond, you&#39;ll lead the teams and vendors that keep our workplaces running at a high standard. You own the full OPEX picture for our workplaces — managing to budget, forecasting with rigor, and always bringing cost-saving options to the table. You think in partnerships: working hand-in-hand with Real Estate to draw the line between Landlord scope and ours and with Development Planners to set long-term standards that drive operational efficiency downstream. You&#39;re a people leader at heart, a sharp cross-functional partner, and you&#39;ll flex to support services in our production areas when the mission calls for it. You take immense pride in your craft, and that pride shows up everywhere — in workplaces that run well, employees who feel taken care of, and an operations function that scales like a well-oiled machine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead and develop operations teams across multiple workplaces to support ongoing day-to-day needs, including office management, culinary/snacks, janitorial, groundskeeping, and related services. Define and own third-party vendor strategy across all service categories, ensuring consistent quality, reliability, and cost-effectiveness across the portfolio. Own the full OPEX budget for our workplaces, reporting out on forecast vs. budget regularly and surfacing cost-saving options. Partner hand-in-hand with the Real Estate team to define what work scope is the Landlord&#39;s responsibility versus ours. Partner hand-in-hand with Development Planners to develop long-term standards that support operational efficiencies downstream. Build scalable operations standards and processes that support growth into additional sites while maintaining a strong employee experience across all spaces. Support services within production areas as needed. Serve as a people leader and cross-functional partner inside and outside Facilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in workplace operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;People management experience, including developing and growing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to own and manage a full OPEX budget, including forecasting and cost-saving identification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to define and manage third-party vendor strategy across multiple service categories&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with real estate on lease scope (Landlord vs. tenant responsibilities)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build scalable operations standards and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of delivering a strong employee experience across multiple sites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience scaling a workplace operations function into new sites in a high-growth environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with office management, culinary, janitorial, and groundskeeping service categories&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting secure environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting services within production or manufacturing areas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OTHER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work Location - This position will be onsite 4 to 5 days per week at our Long Beach, CA facility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Base Salary: $145,000-$210,000&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity + Benefits including Health, Dental, Vision, HRA/HSA options, PTO and paid holidays, 401K, Parental Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Your actual level and base salary will be determined on a case-by-case basis and may vary based on the following considerations: job-related knowledge and skills, education and experience.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;To conform to U.S. Government space technology export regulations, including the International Traffic in Arms Regulations (ITAR) you must be a U.S. citizen, lawful permanent resident of the U.S., protected individual as defined by 8 U.S.C. 1324b(a)(3), or eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;True Anomaly is committed to equal employment opportunity on any basis protected by applicable state and federal laws. If you have a disability or additional need that requires accommodation, please do not hesitate to let us know.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To protect candidates and our company from application fraud and impersonation, we use third-party tools to verify applicant identity and detect fraudulent applications. Learn more in our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.trueanomaly.space/legal/privacy-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The future of aerospace and defense starts here.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ursa Major was founded to revolutionize how America and its allies access and apply high-performance propulsion, from hypersonics to solid rocket motors, satellite maneuvering and launch. We design and deliver propulsion and defense systems that solve the most urgent and critical national security demands.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Director, Quality is the senior quality leader for Ursa Major. This leader is accountable for product quality, quality compliance, and the effectiveness of the Quality Management System across all sites and product lines, including solid rocket motors, hypersonic propulsion, in-space propulsion, and avionics. Reporting to the Chief Safety and Risk Officer, the Sr. Director serves as the company’s senior quality representative to DCMA, government customers, and prime contractors. They will build the program and customer-facing quality capability Ursa Major needs as it scales from development into rate production and operates as a public company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role leads the full quality organization, including quality control, inspection, metrology and calibration, quality systems, and product quality engineering, with full authority to shape its structure as the business grows. The ideal candidate knows what prime-level quality looks like and how to deliver it at startup speed, scaling rigor to risk rather than adding bureaucracy. This is a senior leadership role, but it is also a hands-on one: we expect this leader to roll up their sleeves, lead from the front, and work in the trenches alongside the team as we scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quality Leadership &amp;amp; Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Ursa Major’s quality strategy, objectives, budget, and organization, structuring and developing the quality team to support growth across all product lines and sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a culture of quality where every function owns quality and builds it into design, sourcing, manufacturing, and delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Match quality rigor to program maturity: move at the speed development programs require while meeting the full expectations of mature defense and prime customer programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Government &amp;amp; Prime Customer Quality&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as Ursa Major’s senior quality representative to DCMA, government customers, prime contractors, and certification bodies, building trust-based relationships with DCMA quality assurance representatives and customer quality organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead quality across Ursa Major’s business models: all-up-round deliveries directly to the U.S. government, SRM and propulsion deliveries as a supplier to defense primes, and in-space propulsion systems for satellite and spacecraft customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build an organization capable of reviewing proposals and contracts for quality requirements, including FAR/DFARS quality clauses and customer-specific requirements, and ensure they flow down and implemented across design, purchasing, manufacturing, inspection, and delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own government source inspection, product acceptance, and customer audit readiness, including WAWF acceptance, government first article approval, and witnessed lot acceptance testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with material control to 3nsure effective control of government-furnished property and material under FAR 52.245-1, and support DCMA property management system reviews in partnership with Supply Chain and Contracts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the company’s response to customer corrective action requests, audit findings, and quality escapes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Program Quality&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build Ursa Major’s program quality function, providing dedicated quality ownership for major programs and customers from contract award through delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own contractual quality deliverables and commitments, including first article inspection reports, acceptance data packages, certificates of conformance, as-built records, and customer witness and hold points, and represent quality in program reviews and customer meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quality Systems &amp;amp; Product Quality&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the AS9100 Quality Management System and scale it across sites and product lines, including certification and audits, management review, nonconformance and Material Review Board, corrective action, and Nadcap accreditation of special processes where customers require it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain effective controls for configuration, traceability, quality records, foreign object prevention, and counterfeit parts prevention, including GIDEP reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering and Mission Assurance on design reviews, qualification, first article, and production readiness, and support a disciplined production rate ramp across solid rocket motors, hydrazine satellite propulsion systems, and potential future liquid-engine all-up rounds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In partnership with Safety, ensure quality controls fit energetics manufacturing, including propellant processing, cast-cure operations, and lot control and traceability of energetic materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure quality coverage for avionics and electronics, including electronics assembly workmanship and software and firmware quality, developing the team expertise needed as the avionics business grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape supplier quality through influence rather than ownership: partner with Procurement, which owns supplier engineering, to set supplier quality requirements and flowdowns, weigh in on the selection and approval of critical suppliers, and drive resolution of supplier escapes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Authority &amp;amp; Public Company Governance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold authority to stop production, testing, acceptance, or shipment when product conformity, safety, or contractual compliance may be compromised, with an independent escalation path to the CEO and Business Unit President.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cost of poor quality reduction and continuous improvement: partner with Finance to accurately capture scrap, rework, and warranty costs in line with public company financial controls and use that data to drive measurable improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Engineering or a related technical field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of progressive quality experience in aerospace, defense, or similarly regulated manufacturing, including 5+ years in senior quality leadership building, scaling, and leading quality organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct, hands-on experience working with DCMA, including quality surveillance, government source inspection, and corrective action requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience serving U.S. government and prime contractor customers, including contract quality requirements, FAR/DFARS quality clauses, requirement flowdowns, and customer audits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience leading and sustaining an AS9100-certified Quality Management System.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading quality through the transition from development into production and rate ramp.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of right-sizing quality rigor to risk, maintaining compliance and product integrity without slowing execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build and sustain a strong culture of quality, where ownership of quality extends well beyond the quality organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with solid rocket motors, energetic materials, propellant processing, munitions, or tactical propulsion (strongly preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Public company experience (strongly preferred), including board-level reporting or supporting public company internal controls; experience through an IPO is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in both a traditional prime and a startup or non-traditional defense environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with avionics and electronics quality, such as electronics workmanship standards (IPC J-STD-001, IPC-A-610), ESD control, and software and firmware quality assurance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master’s degree in Engineering, Business, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ASQ CMQ/OE, CQE, or CQA certification, or AS9100 lead auditor experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working Conditions / Physical Demands&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work performed in office, laboratory, and manufacturing environments, including hazardous and energetic operations areas that require personal protective equipment and adherence to explosives safety and site security protocols.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to sit or stand for extended periods and work on a computer for prolonged durations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Occasionally required to lift up to 25 pounds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel up to 25% to Ursa Major sites, customers, suppliers, and government facilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Colorado law requires us to tell you the base compensation range of this role, which is $225,000 - $275,000, determined by your education, experience, knowledge, skills, and abilities. What we &lt;em&gt;can’t&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;quantify for you are the exciting challenges, supportive team, and amazing culture we enjoy.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Classification: Full-time Exempt&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits Include: (Please note, Interns are not eligible for benefits)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited PTO - Vacation, Sick, Personal, and Bereavement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid Parental and Adoptive Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, Dental and Vision Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tax Advantage Accounts (HSA/FSA)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employer Paid Short and Long Term Disability, Basic Life, AD&amp;amp;D&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional Benefit Options Including Voluntary Life and Emergency Medical Transport&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EAP Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retirement Savings Plan - 401k with Company Match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How To Apply:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Interested candidates are encouraged to apply by filling out the application below and clicking &quot;Submit Application&quot;. This position will be posted for a minimum of 3 days and will remain open until filled or adjusted based on the volume of applicants.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NOTE: &lt;/strong&gt;Research suggests that women and BIPOC individuals may self-select out of opportunities if they don&#39;t meet 100% of the job requirements. We encourage anyone who believes they have the skills and the drive necessary to succeed here to apply for this role.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must be a U.S. Person (this includes U.S. Citizens and Permanent Residents).&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Eligibility to obtain and maintain a U.S. Security Clearance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;em&gt;We’re an equal-opportunity employer. You will be considered for employment without attention to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran, or disability status.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;No outside recruiters, please.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;CHAOS Industries is redefining modern defense with a multi-product portfolio that gives the ultimate advantage—domain dominance. The company&#39;s products are powered by Coherent Distributed Networks (CDN™), empowering warfighters, commercial air operators, and border protection teams to act faster, adapt rapidly, and stay ahead of evolving threats.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CHAOS Industries was founded in 2022 and has raised a total of $1 billion in funding from leading investors, including 8VC, Accel, and Valor Equity Partners. The company is headquartered in Los Angeles, with offices in Washington, D.C., San Francisco, San Diego, Seattle, and London. For more information, please visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chaosinc.com&quot;&gt;www.chaosinc.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As CHAOS Industries scales production of advanced defense systems, manufacturing execution becomes a critical competitive advantage. We are seeking a Chief of Staff, Manufacturing to serve as a force multiplier for our manufacturing organization—driving strategic initiatives, solving complex operational challenges, and ensuring critical priorities translate into measurable outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working closely with Manufacturing Leadership, Supply Chain, Engineering, Quality, Finance, and Program Management, you will lead high-impact projects that improve throughput, enable scale, and strengthen operational performance across the business. This is a builder’s role: you will identify bottlenecks, develop solutions, and drive execution in areas that do not neatly fit within existing organizational boundaries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate combines the structured thinking and analytical rigor of a top-tier consulting background with the ownership mindset and bias for action required to build in a fast-paced manufacturing environment. This is a 0-to-1 role: you will be standing up structure, owning cross-functional work that has no home yet, and acting as connective tissue across a leadership team that is still being built—not optimizing a machine that already runs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;High performers in this role are positioned to move into manufacturing leadership seats as the organization scales.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and run the manufacturing operating rhythm—performance reviews, operating mechanisms, and decision forums that create accountability across functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own cross-functional work that does not yet have a clear home: identify bottlenecks, run root-cause analyses, drive issues to closure, and stand up the structure to keep them closed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build executive-level analyses, business cases, and decision-support materials that inform strategic and operational decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the metrics backbone—throughput, quality, labor, capacity, and on-time delivery reporting—into a single operating picture leadership can run on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support capacity planning, facility expansion, and production ramp efforts as a hands-on project owner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead special, high-priority initiatives on behalf of manufacturing leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree and 7+ years of experience spanning both a strategy/consulting environment and an operating role where you owned execution and results (manufacturing, industrial, or operations).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading complex, cross-functional initiatives from problem definition through implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and structured problem-solving capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing executive-level presentations, analyses, and recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to operate independently in fast-paced, ambiguous environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to drive outcomes through influence rather than positional authority; this role leads cross-functional work without direct reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication, stakeholder management, and project leadership skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;U.S. citizenship is required: this role accesses export-controlled information and requires a U.S. Department of Defense (DoD) Secret security clearance—current, or the ability to obtain and maintain one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a top-tier consulting firm such as McKinsey, Bain, BCG, Deloitte, Oliver Wyman, LEK, or Accenture Strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting manufacturing, industrial, supply chain, aerospace, defense, or other operationally intensive organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading operational excellence, business transformation, production scaling, or organizational effectiveness initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with manufacturing operations, production systems, supply chain management, or industrial engineering principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with senior executives and leadership teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active U.S. Department of Defense Secret or Top Secret security clearance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why CHAOS?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Health Benefits: &lt;/strong&gt;Medical, dental, and vision benefits 100% paid for by the company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional benefits&lt;/strong&gt;: 401k (+ 50% company match up to 6% of pay), FSA, HSA, life insurance, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Perks: &lt;/strong&gt;Free daily lunch, ‘No meeting Fridays’, unlimited PTO, casual dress code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation Components:&lt;/strong&gt; Competitive base salaries, generous pre-IPO stock option grants, relocation assistance, and (coming soon!) annual bonuses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Growth: &lt;/strong&gt;350 employees and counting across 5 global offices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary Range: $150,000 - $220,000&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The stated compensation range reflects only the targeted base compensation range and excludes additional earnings such as bonus, equity, and benefits. If your compensation requirements fall outside of the range, we still encourage you to apply. The salary range for this role is an estimate based on a range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
