&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prime Medicine is a leading biotechnology company dedicated to creating and delivering the next generation of gene editing therapies to patients. The Company is leveraging its proprietary Prime Editing platform, a versatile, precise and efficient gene editing technology, to develop a new class of differentiated, one-time, potentially curative genetic therapies. Designed to make only the right edit at the right position within a gene while minimizing unwanted DNA modifications, Prime Editors have the potential to repair almost all types of genetic mutations and work in many different tissues, organs and cell types. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prime Medicine is currently progressing a diversified portfolio of investigational therapeutic programs organized around our core areas of focus: hematology, immunology &amp;amp; oncology, liver and lung. Across each core area, Prime Medicine is focused initially on a set of high value programs, each targeting a disease with well-understood biology and a clearly defined clinical development and regulatory path, and each expected to provide the foundation for expansion into additional opportunities. For more information, please visit &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.primemedicine.com/&quot;&gt;www.primemedicine.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Prime Medicine is a clinical-stage biotechnology company creating the next generation of gene editing therapies. Our Prime Editing platform is versatile, precise, and efficient, with the potential to address more than 90% of known disease-causing genetic mutations. We have three programs in the clinic: an ex vivo cell therapy for an ultra-rare disease advancing toward a Biologics License Application (BLA), and two in vivo liver-targeting LNP Prime Editor programs, with more in development. We are a mission-driven team working in a lean, fast-moving environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Position Overview&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting directly to the Chief Technology Officer, the Executive Director of Supply Chain and External Manufacturing is a member of the Technology, Development and Operations (TDO) leadership team. You will own Prime Medicine’s end-to-end supply chain, from raw materials through clinical supply and commercialization, with direct accountability for materials management and for supporting internal planning and manufacturing needs. You will manage our external manufacturing partners, lead a highly functional lean team, and serve as the primary partner to Finance for TDO external spend. We are looking for a leader who embraces AI as a core part of how supply chain and external manufacturing run at Prime Medicine, from forecasting and materials visibility to partner performance and cost modeling. This role is for someone who thrives in ambiguity, is energized by building, and pairs strategic thinking with hands-on execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Primary Responsibilities&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;Partner with the CTO and TDO leadership to define manufacturing and supply chain strategy, including network design, make-vs-buy decisions, and partner selection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-enabled operations. &lt;/strong&gt;Lead the use of AI and digital tools across supply chain and external manufacturing, including demand forecasting, materials and inventory visibility, partner performance monitoring, contract and cost modeling, and logistics tracking, as well as keeping the function ahead of new tools as they emerge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Materials management. &lt;/strong&gt;Own materials management across the portfolio, including forecasting, sourcing, purchasing, and inventory of raw materials, critical starting materials, and components, so materials are available on time for each program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Planning and supply operations. &lt;/strong&gt;Support internal planning and the manufacturing needs of each program; deliver labeling, packaging, shipping, and cell therapy logistics on time and in full; and resolve supply risks before they affect timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;External manufacturing and partners. &lt;/strong&gt;Build and manage a network of CDMOs, CROs, and critical suppliers, including contracts, governance, performance, and qualification of new partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clinical and commercial readiness. &lt;/strong&gt;Ensure supply chain documentation and external site readiness support IND and BLA submissions, working with CMC, Regulatory, Quality, Non-clinical Development, Clinical, and program teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;Own TDO budget development for external spend, cost projections, and financial reporting in close partnership with functional leaders and Finance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;. Lead, coach, and inspire your team of supply chain/external manufacturing professionals and indirect colleagues across TDO; foster a culture of accountability, continuous improvement, and collaborative problem-solving and goal attainment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in a relevant technical discipline; advanced degree (MS, MBA, or PhD) preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15–20+ years of progressive experience in supply chain, technical operations, external manufacturing, process development, or MSAT within biotech or pharma&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct ownership of materials management and clinical supply for clinical-stage programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing CDMOs and CROs, including negotiating MSAs and SOWs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cell therapy and/or LNP or nucleic acid programs; experience supporting IND/CTA and BLA/MAA submissions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Financial acumen, including ownership of operating budgets and multi-year cost projections&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of implementing AI or digital tools that improved forecasting, visibility, or decision-making in supply chain or operations, and of changing how teams work as a result&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong change management, project management, and communication skills, with the ability to build trust with partners, Finance, and senior leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plus: lean, fast-moving biotech; ultra-rare disease or small patient population experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Why Prime Medicine&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your work will matter: our programs have the potential to be curative therapies for patients with no other options, and this role directly enables that. You will be part of the TDO leadership team, with direct access to the CTO and interact with other Executive leaders, and you will shape how AI is applied to supply chain and manufacturing at a company where it is a growing priority. You will have ownership from day one in building how Prime Medicine delivers for patients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prime Medicine is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability, veteran status, or any other classification protected by law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Location: Cambridge, MA | Reports to: Chief Technology Officer | TDO Leadership Team Member&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The pay range reflects the full-time base salary range we expect to pay for this role at the time of posting. Base pay will be determined based on several factors including, but not limited to, relevant experience, skills, and education. This role is eligible for an annual short-term incentive award (e.g., bonus) and an annual long-term incentive award (e.g., equity).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prime Medicine offers a comprehensive Total Rewards package with robust health, financial, and wellness benefits—including medical, dental, vision, life insurance, a 401(k) match, and equity programs—along with generous paid time off, wellness days, and company-wide recharge breaks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our commitment to employee well-being reflects our belief that when we care for our people, we strengthen our ability to put patients first and make meaningful impact together.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;U.S. Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$295,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$312,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Prime Medicine is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability, veteran status, or any other classification protected by law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;About&amp;nbsp;Re:Build&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;At&amp;nbsp;Re:Build, our mission is to ensure the next generation of important products are made, at scale, in America. We are laying the foundation for a better future for our customers, employees, and communities by revitalizing America&#39;s manufacturing base and creating meaningful jobs across the country, including in historically deindustrialized regions.&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;We operate an advanced, end-to-end manufacturing platform that partners with industrial companies and innovators to take products from first concept to full-scale production in critical verticals including aerospace and defense, electrification, medical, energy and environment, and robotics and automation.&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;The way we operate is as important as the work we do. It&#39;s guided by The&amp;nbsp;Re:Build&amp;nbsp;Way, 16 principles that shape how we collaborate with each other, partner with our customers and vendors, and contribute to the communities where we operate.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;(link to&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://rebuildmanufacturing.com/about/rebuild-way/&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The Re:Build Way principles&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Re:Build Composite Resources&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Composite Resources, a Re:Build Manufacturing company, is an innovative, rapidly growing manufacturer of composite components and tooling located in Rock Hill, SC. Our constantly evolving portfolio of projects includes parts and assemblies for clients in the aerospace and defense industries. At Composite Resources, we embrace a culture defined by teamwork, ownership, and accountability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Composite Resources is looking for a strategic, hands-on Quality leader ready to build a quality function from the ground up during a period of significant growth. You&#39;ve successfully led a facility or special process through NADCAP certification before and know what it takes to go from readiness assessment to accreditation. You&#39;re comfortable operating at the executive level — shaping strategy and reporting directly to the President — while still rolling up your sleeves to solve problems on the floor.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You bring experience in quality systems, APQP, and Lean/Six Sigma in manufacturing, ideally within composites or aerospace. You&#39;re energized by the challenge of building a quality strategy that works for both a fast-moving, high-mix prototyping operation and a higher-volume, cost-disciplined production site — with the opportunity to build your own team and establish quality as a true competitive advantage.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Get To Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Lead the organization&#39;s achievement of NADCAP certification at the new site — owning the roadmap, readiness assessments, gap closure, audit prep, and accreditation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Build and lead a growing Quality team to support expansion across two facilities over the next five years.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Define a culture of quality and set department goals aligned with company objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Implement and maintain AS9100, ISO, NADCAP, and other aerospace/composites certifications, including internal, compliance, and supplier audits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Architect quality strategies tailored to two environments — balancing fast-paced prototyping with cost-efficient, higher-volume production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Partner with other departments to plan, implement, and improve quality programs supporting business goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Track quality metrics and turn data/trends into improvement actions with cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Apply SPC, analytics, AI tools, and Lean/A3 problem-solving to drive process improvement and error prevention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Engage with customers on gate reviews, documentation, deviation approvals, engineering changes, and part quality concerns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Ensure timely completion of quality documentation (ballooned drawings, PFMEAs, control plans, capability studies, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring To The Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Required:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Quality Systems, Engineering, or related field, or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Hands-on experience successfully achieving NADCAP certification for a site or special process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;5+ years in Quality Systems, APQP, Lean/Six Sigma, and large-scale project management in manufacturing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;2+ years in a leadership role, with proven success building and developing a quality team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Strong knowledge of AS9100 and NADCAP requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Strong organizational, analytical, and problem-solving skills; ability to drive change with minimal direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Ability to communicate quality objectives/requirements effectively and negotiate with customers and vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Willingness to work flexibly, including occasional travel between facilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Strongly Preferred:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Composites and aerospace manufacturing experience, including both prototype and high-volume environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Familiarity with ISO9000, ISO13485, and ITAR.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Knowledge of gauging, metrology, and CMM programming/software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Experience leveraging AI and technology to improve quality efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
