&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;About&amp;nbsp;Re:Build&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;At&amp;nbsp;Re:Build, our mission is to ensure the next generation of important products are made, at scale, in America. We are laying the foundation for a better future for our customers, employees, and communities by revitalizing America&#39;s manufacturing base and creating meaningful jobs across the country, including in historically deindustrialized regions.&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;We operate an advanced, end-to-end manufacturing platform that partners with industrial companies and innovators to take products from first concept to full-scale production in critical verticals including aerospace and defense, electrification, medical, energy and environment, and robotics and automation.&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;The way we operate is as important as the work we do. It&#39;s guided by The&amp;nbsp;Re:Build&amp;nbsp;Way, 16 principles that shape how we collaborate with each other, partner with our customers and vendors, and contribute to the communities where we operate.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;(link to&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://rebuildmanufacturing.com/about/rebuild-way/&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The Re:Build Way principles&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Re:Build Composite Resources&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Composite Resources, a Re:Build Manufacturing company, is an innovative, rapidly growing manufacturer of composite components and tooling located in Rock Hill, SC. Our constantly evolving portfolio of projects includes parts and assemblies for clients in the aerospace and defense industries. At Composite Resources, we embrace a culture defined by teamwork, ownership, and accountability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Composite Resources is looking for a strategic, hands-on Quality leader ready to build a quality function from the ground up during a period of significant growth. You&#39;ve successfully led a facility or special process through NADCAP certification before and know what it takes to go from readiness assessment to accreditation. You&#39;re comfortable operating at the executive level — shaping strategy and reporting directly to the President — while still rolling up your sleeves to solve problems on the floor.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You bring experience in quality systems, APQP, and Lean/Six Sigma in manufacturing, ideally within composites or aerospace. You&#39;re energized by the challenge of building a quality strategy that works for both a fast-moving, high-mix prototyping operation and a higher-volume, cost-disciplined production site — with the opportunity to build your own team and establish quality as a true competitive advantage.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Get To Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Lead the organization&#39;s achievement of NADCAP certification at the new site — owning the roadmap, readiness assessments, gap closure, audit prep, and accreditation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Build and lead a growing Quality team to support expansion across two facilities over the next five years.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Define a culture of quality and set department goals aligned with company objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Implement and maintain AS9100, ISO, NADCAP, and other aerospace/composites certifications, including internal, compliance, and supplier audits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Architect quality strategies tailored to two environments — balancing fast-paced prototyping with cost-efficient, higher-volume production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Partner with other departments to plan, implement, and improve quality programs supporting business goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Track quality metrics and turn data/trends into improvement actions with cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Apply SPC, analytics, AI tools, and Lean/A3 problem-solving to drive process improvement and error prevention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Engage with customers on gate reviews, documentation, deviation approvals, engineering changes, and part quality concerns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Ensure timely completion of quality documentation (ballooned drawings, PFMEAs, control plans, capability studies, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring To The Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Required:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Quality Systems, Engineering, or related field, or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Hands-on experience successfully achieving NADCAP certification for a site or special process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;5+ years in Quality Systems, APQP, Lean/Six Sigma, and large-scale project management in manufacturing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;2+ years in a leadership role, with proven success building and developing a quality team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Strong knowledge of AS9100 and NADCAP requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Strong organizational, analytical, and problem-solving skills; ability to drive change with minimal direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Ability to communicate quality objectives/requirements effectively and negotiate with customers and vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Willingness to work flexibly, including occasional travel between facilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Strongly Preferred:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Composites and aerospace manufacturing experience, including both prototype and high-volume environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Familiarity with ISO9000, ISO13485, and ITAR.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Knowledge of gauging, metrology, and CMM programming/software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-start &quot;&gt;Experience leveraging AI and technology to improve quality efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this position is $116,616 – $174,924.75 per year. This range represents the Company’s good faith estimate of the base compensation for this role at the time of posting.&amp;nbsp; Actual compensation will be determined based on several factors, including but not limited to relevant experience, skills, qualifications, internal equity, and geographic location. In addition to base salary, this role may be eligible for annual incentive compensation and/or long-term incentives, subject to Company plans. The Company offers a comprehensive benefits package including medical, dental, vision, retirement, paid time off, and other benefits.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The BIG payoff&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a company who is going to make a difference in the industries and the communities in which we choose to operate.&amp;nbsp; Every employee of Re:Build will share ownership in the company and will share in the financial rewards of the success we achieve together, at all levels of the company!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We want to work with people that reflect the communities in which we operate&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Re:Build Manufacturing is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action employer. We do not discriminate based upon race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, veteran status, marital status, parental status, cultural background, organizational level, work styles, tenure and life experiences. Or for any other reason.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Re:Build is committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities in our job application procedures. If you need assistance or an accommodation due to a disability, you may contact us at accommodations.ta@ReBuildmanufacturing.com or you may call us at 617.909.6275.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;About&amp;nbsp;Re:Build&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;At&amp;nbsp;Re:Build, our mission is to ensure the next generation of important products are made, at scale, in America. We are laying the foundation for a better future for our customers, employees, and communities by revitalizing America&#39;s manufacturing base and creating meaningful jobs across the country, including in historically deindustrialized regions.&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;We operate an advanced, end-to-end manufacturing platform that partners with industrial companies and innovators to take products from first concept to full-scale production in critical verticals including aerospace and defense, electrification, medical, energy and environment, and robotics and automation.&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;The way we operate is as important as the work we do. It&#39;s guided by The&amp;nbsp;Re:Build&amp;nbsp;Way, 16 principles that shape how we collaborate with each other, partner with our customers and vendors, and contribute to the communities where we operate.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;(link to&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://rebuildmanufacturing.com/about/rebuild-way/&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The Re:Build Way principles&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Re:Build Harness Solutions is looking for an experienced manufacturing leader to lead wire harness operations at our Kalamazoo, Michigan facility. You bring direct experience in wire harness, cable assembly, or electro-mechanical manufacturing and know how to build safe, reliable operations that deliver on quality, cost, and customer commitments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;You are a hands-on, metrics-driven leader who develops strong teams and scalable manufacturing systems. You use measures such as OEE, first-pass yield, cycle time, labor efficiency, safety, and on-time delivery to drive improvement and make informed decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;This is an opportunity to help build a digitally integrated wire harness operation and establish the processes, technology, and workforce capabilities needed to support continued growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Get To Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead&lt;/strong&gt; daily manufacturing operations with accountability for safety, quality, delivery, cost, and customer priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive&lt;/strong&gt; production performance using KPIs including OEE, first-pass yield, on-time delivery, cycle time, and labor efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optimize&lt;/strong&gt; wire harness processes including cutting, stripping, crimping, soldering, assembly, testing, and inspection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Implement&lt;/strong&gt; wire processing equipment, automated systems, smartBuild formboards, tooling, and digital manufacturing technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead&lt;/strong&gt; Lean continuous improvement efforts to reduce waste, improve quality, and increase production efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner&lt;/strong&gt; with Engineering on manufacturability, capacity, production requirements, and process improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and develop&lt;/strong&gt; a high-performing team of supervisors, engineers, technicians, and production operators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own&lt;/strong&gt; plant safety, quality, and compliance, including applicable IPC/WHMA-A-620, AS9100, ISO 13485, and ITAR requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead&lt;/strong&gt; root cause analysis, corrective actions, quality audits, inspection, and testing activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage&lt;/strong&gt; key plant financial drivers, capital equipment investments, manufacturing costs, and capacity planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support&lt;/strong&gt; customer requirements, quoting, business reviews, and strategic growth initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring To The Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of manufacturing operations experience, including 5+ years in plant or production management leading teams of 20+.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct wire harness, cable assembly, or electro-mechanical manufacturing experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience scaling low-volume, high-mix operations and improving quality, cost, and delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of wire cutting, stripping, crimping, soldering, assembly, testing, and wire harness workmanship standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with wire processing equipment such as Komax, Schleuniger, or equivalent systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of IPC/WHMA-A-620 and familiarity with ITAR-controlled manufacturing environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Lean manufacturing and structured problem-solving experience, including 5S, standard work, visual management, A3, or 8D.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ERP/MES systems, production metrics, capacity planning, scheduling, and manufacturing flow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build teams, coach employees, and lead through growth or operational transformation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work onsite in Kalamazoo, Michigan and travel up to 10%.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;IPC/WHMA-A-620 Certified IPC Specialist or Trainer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AS9100 or ISO 9001 Lead Auditor certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lean Six Sigma Green Belt or Black Belt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;OSHA certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this position is $120,000 – $180,000 per year. This range represents the Company’s good faith estimate of the base compensation for this role at the time of posting.&amp;nbsp; Actual compensation will be determined based on several factors, including but not limited to relevant experience, skills, qualifications, internal equity, and geographic location. In addition to base salary, this role may be eligible for annual incentive compensation and/or long-term incentives, subject to Company plans. The Company offers a comprehensive benefits package including medical, dental, vision, retirement, paid time off, and other benefits.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The BIG payoff&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a company who is going to make a difference in the industries and the communities in which we choose to operate.&amp;nbsp; Every employee of Re:Build will share ownership in the company and will share in the financial rewards of the success we achieve together, at all levels of the company!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We want to work with people that reflect the communities in which we operate&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Re:Build Manufacturing is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action employer. We do not discriminate based upon race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, veteran status, marital status, parental status, cultural background, organizational level, work styles, tenure and life experiences. Or for any other reason.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Re:Build is committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities in our job application procedures. If you need assistance or an accommodation due to a disability, you may contact us at accommodations.ta@ReBuildmanufacturing.com or you may call us at 617.909.6275.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;DIRECTOR, POWER PLANT OPERATIONS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Director, Memphis Power Plant Operations provides strategic and operational leadership for the gas turbine power generation facility supporting SpaceXSI&#39;s Colossus data center campus in Memphis, Tennessee. This role oversees all plant operations, maintenance, commissioning, and continued construction/expansion of the dedicated power plant, with full ownership of delivering reliable, high-availability electrical power to the Colossus AI training clusters. The position is responsible for driving operational excellence, ensuring 24/7 power reliability and quality, safety, environmental compliance, and leading cross-functional teams to achieve aggressive scale-up, availability, cost, and schedule objectives in a high-growth, fast-paced environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strategic and operational leadership for the Memphis gas turbine power plant, including 24/7 operations, maintenance, commissioning, and ongoing construction and capacity expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end delivery of electrical power to the Colossus data center sites, ensuring industry-leading reliability, availability, power quality, and redundancy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead multidisciplinary teams of operators, maintenance technicians, engineers, contractors, and support staff in a 24/7 operational and construction environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee plant performance, commissioning, testing, and seamless integration with data center electrical infrastructure and load&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute comprehensive operations and maintenance strategies, including preventative/predictive maintenance, outage planning, hot gas path management, and OEM coordination for gas turbines, generators, balance of plant, and high-voltage electrical systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage concurrent construction, equipment installation, civil works, and phased capacity expansions while maintaining safe, reliable operation of the existing plant&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure full compliance with environmental, safety, and regulatory requirements, including air permits, emissions controls, TDEC, EPA, OSHA, and local authorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with SpaceXSI data center operations, engineering, fuel suppliers, OEMs, utilities, and regulatory agencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Formulate and execute operating budgets, fuel management, O&amp;amp;M, capital projects, and annual operating plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvement in plant availability, heat rate, emissions, cost, safety metrics, and operational processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and promote a culture of uncompromising safety, accountability, operational excellence, rapid execution, and collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the site leader and primary representative to the Memphis community, regulators, and stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, develop, coach, and retain high-performing talent; manage staffing, resource allocation, and contractor oversight for both operations and construction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in mechanical, electrical, or other engineering discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in power generation operations, plant management, or industrial or aerospace operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of leadership experience managing teams of operators, technicians, and engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating or managing gas turbine power plants (simple cycle or combined cycle)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing large-scale gas turbine facilities (100 MW+), preferably with high-availability critical power applications (data centers, industrial, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of achieving and sustaining high plant availability, reliability, and low forced outage rates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with plant construction, commissioning, start-up, and concurrent operations/expansion of gas turbine facilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of gas turbine technology (aeroderivative and/or heavy-duty frames), performance optimization, emissions controls (SCR, etc.), and balance of plant systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with high-voltage electrical systems, generators, switchgear, protection, and data center or industrial interconnection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of environmental permitting, air quality compliance, and regulatory reporting for combustion turbines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fast-paced, high-growth environments requiring simultaneous operations and major construction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage budgets, fuel costs, contractors, and complex stakeholder relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent oral and written communication, leadership, and interpersonal skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unfazed by major, abrupt changes in strategic direction or aggressive timelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in a demanding, autonomously driven, start-up atmosphere&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to support and supervise plant operations and construction outside of normal business hours, including nights, weekends, and on-call response&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be based at the Memphis, TN site&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work extended hours as needed to support plant reliability and construction milestones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;General physical fitness required; ability to walk the plant site, access equipment, and work in industrial/outdoor environments (heat, noise, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

